# Dock layout integrity (Play / CaseContextPanel)

The floating command dock has three independent view states: **hidden** (`dockHidden`),
**collapsed** (`dockCollapsed`, chrome-only), and **expanded** (full body). Several
times this has silently broken so the dock opens empty and cannot be expanded.
These are the non-negotiable rules.

## Symptom signature (if you see this, it's this bug)
- Every case opens with an **empty / collapsed** dock (header + tabs, no body).
- Clicking "Expand panel" / a tab does nothing — the dock **snaps back collapsed**.
- `.case-context-body-wrap` measures **height 0** while `dockCollapsed` is false.

## Rule 1 — Never put a dockLayout-dependent callback in an effect dep array
`expandDockPanel` / `collapseDockPanel` are `useCallback`s that depend on `dockLayout`.
`usePlayDockLayout.persist()` calls `setLayout()`, so **`dockLayout` gets a new reference
on every collapse/expand**. If you list `collapseDockPanel` (or `expandDockPanel`) in a
`useEffect` dependency array, that effect **re-fires on every layout change** → an expand
immediately triggers a re-collapse (infinite fight) and corrupts the saved height.

✅ Use a ref: `collapseDockPanelRef` / `expandDockPanelRef` (assigned every render), and
depend only on the real trigger (`caseData?.id`, `teachMeMode`).

```js
const collapseDockPanelRef = useRef(collapseDockPanel);
collapseDockPanelRef.current = collapseDockPanel;
// effect:
useEffect(() => {
  if (!caseData?.id) return;
  if (teachMeMode) collapseDockPanelRef.current();
  else expandDockPanelRef.current();
  // eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps
}, [caseData?.id, teachMeMode]);
```

## Rule 2 — Normal play opens EXPANDED; only teach-me opens collapsed
The case-load effect must be conditional. **Do not** make it unconditionally
`collapseDockPanel()`. (This is exactly what the 2026-06 study→main sync did and it
shipped the empty-dock bug to main.)

## Rule 3 — Expand/collapse must round-trip the FULL layout
`collapseDockPanel` zeroes `clinicalPx`/`stacksListPx` and shrinks `height`. If
`expandDockPanel` only restores `height`, the body stays **0px**. Snapshot the whole
layout on collapse and restore the whole layout on expand:
- Collapse: `expandedDockLayoutRef.current = { ...dockLayout }` **only when genuinely
  expanded** (`height > DOCK_CHROME_COLLAPSED_HEIGHT + 4`), then persist the collapsed
  geometry with **`{ write: false }`** so localStorage keeps the user's expanded size.
- Expand: restore the snapshot; if none and currently collapsed, fall back to
  `defaultPlayDockLayout()` so a corrupted/collapsed saved layout can still open.

## Rule 4 — readPlayDockLayout only self-heals clinicalPx, NOT height
`clinicalPx: Number(parsed.clinicalPx) || base.clinicalPx` heals a stored `0`. But
`height` is kept if truthy, so a persisted collapsed height (148) **sticks across reloads**.
That's why Rule 3 uses `write:false` on collapse — never persist collapsed height.

## Rule 5 — Smoke test after ANY dock change or study→main sync
On a **normal** (non-teach) case at `:5174`:
1. Resume/enter a case → dock opens **expanded**, `.case-context-body-wrap` height > 0.
2. Single-click dock handle → collapses. Sidebar button single-click → expands.
3. Double-click sidebar button → hides; single-click → shows, still expanded.
4. Collapse → expand round-trip keeps body height (not 0).

## History
- **2026-06-26**: `788bfaa` (study→main sync) replaced the conditional case-load collapse
  with unconditional `collapseDockPanel()` AND the effect listed `collapseDockPanel` in
  deps → empty dock + re-collapse loop + lossy (height-only) expand. Fixed by Rules 1–3.
